(4000741, 567704, 80912, '<td valign="top">Thanks everyone! I''m really excited about this. (And will try to hold on to the feeling when my next few submissions don''t do nearly as well, lol).<br/> <br/>I had so much fun running around at work holding my camera upside down. As I mentioned in the scores thread - I apparently have found my niche. rofl<br/> <br/>For Judi - this is what''s around the corner (taken w/ a flash so that what''s outside the door isn''t blown out). I held the camera directly under the exit sign.<br/> <br/><a href="//public.fotki.com/Donna21/upside-downtoy-outtakes/aroundthecorner.html" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images28.fotki.com/v1002/photos/1/1194048/5280638/aroundthecorner-th.jpg'', strrpos(''//images28.fotki.com/v1002/photos/1/1194048/5280638/aroundthecorner-th.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images28.fotki.com/v1002/photos/1/1194048/5280638/aroundthecorner-th.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>And some outtakes -<br/> <br/><a href="//public.fotki.com/Donna21/upside-downtoy-outtakes/arch-confusion.html" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images28.fotki.com/v988/photos/1/1194048/5280638/Archconfusion-th.jpg'', strrpos(''//images28.fotki.com/v988/photos/1/1194048/5280638/Archconfusion-th.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images28.fotki.com/v988/photos/1/1194048/5280638/Archconfusion-th.jpg"/></a> I thought this looked like an Escher drawing, but couldn''t edit out the ugly metal railing on top.<br/> <br/><a href="//public.fotki.com/Donna21/upside-downtoy-outtakes/ramps2.html" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images28.fotki.com/v998/photos/1/1194048/5280638/Ramps2-th.jpg'', strrpos(''//images28.fotki.com/v998/photos/1/1194048/5280638/Ramps2-th.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images28.fotki.com/v998/photos/1/1194048/5280638/Ramps2-th.jpg"/></a> The blown out grass (in the top of the window) was the best and the worst part of this.<br/><a href="//public.fotki.com/Donna21/upside-downtoy-outtakes/sm-lightwell.html" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images27.fotki.com/v992/photos/1/1194048/5280638/smLightwell-th.jpg'', strrpos(''//images27.fotki.com/v992/photos/1/1194048/5280638/smLightwell-th.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images27.fotki.com/v992/photos/1/1194048/5280638/smLightwell-th.jpg"/></a> <a href="//public.fotki.com/Donna21/upside-downtoy-outtakes/spaceport.html" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images27.fotki.com/v993/photos/1/1194048/5280638/Spaceport-th.jpg'', strrpos(''//images27.fotki.com/v993/photos/1/1194048/5280638/Spaceport-th.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images27.fotki.com/v993/photos/1/1194048/5280638/Spaceport-th.jpg"/></a> Yes, I work in a very funky building, lol.<br/> <br/><a href="//public.fotki.com/Donna21/upside-downtoy-outtakes/smbridgedbridge.html" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images28.fotki.com/v1001/photos/1/1194048/5280638/smBridgedBridge-th.jpg'', strrpos(''//images28.fotki.com/v1001/photos/1/1194048/5280638/smBridgedBridge-th.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images28.fotki.com/v1001/photos/1/1194048/5280638/smBridgedBridge-th.jpg"/></a> This is the only one I even considered of anything else - and I liked the title better than the shot. I called it "A Bridged Bridge."<br/> <br/>ETA - not sure why the thumbs aren''t working, but the links are.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-08-28 16:02:35.</i></td>', 'Thanks everyone! I''m really excited about this. (And will try to hold on to the feeling when my next few submissions don''t do nearly as well, lol). I had so much fun running around at work holding my camera upside down. As I mentioned in the scores thread - I apparently have found my niche. rofl For Judi - this is what''s around the corner (taken w/ a flash so that what''s outside the door isn''t blown out). I held the camera directly under the exit sign.   And some outtakes -  I thought this looked like an Escher drawing, but couldn''t edit out the ugly metal railing on top.  The blown out grass (in the top of the window) was the best and the worst part of this.  Yes, I work in a very funky building, lol.  This is the only one I even considered of anything else - and I liked the title better than the shot. I called it "A Bridged Bridge." ETA - not sure why the thumbs aren''t working, but the links are.', '2007-08-15 12:31:40.000000', '2007-08-28 17:02:35.000000', 0),
